00132: install temporary interior sound mitigation walls. Interior and exterior alterations and additions.","record_status":"Closed","project_address":"301 MISSION ST C132 94105","block":"3719","lot":"021","open_date":"2020-05-15T00:00:00.000","close_date":"2020-06-24T00:00:00.000","building_permits":"202003167141","applicant":"Rescalvo, Glenn","applicant_org":"Handel Architects","assigned_to_planner":"Heidi Kline","environmental_document_type":"Exemption","environmental_document_date":"8/17/2020","number_of_units_net":"0.0","number_of_market_rate_units":"0","number_of_affordable_units":"0","number_of_units_exist":"0","number_market_rate_units":"0","number_affordable_units_exist":"0","number_of_units_prop":"0","number_market_rate_units_1":"0","number_affordable_units_prop":"0","change_of_use":"No","additions":"CHECKED","demolition":"No","facade_alt":"CHECKED","pim_link":{"url":"https://sfplanninggis.org/pim?search=2020-005022PRJ"}},{"record_id":"2018-004054PRJ","record_type":"PRJ","project_name":"301 MISSION STREET","description":"The proposed scope of work consists of drilling a single rotary-wash boring that will be converted to a monitoring well in the sidewalk of Fremont Street near Millennium Tower (301 Mission Street). The boring will be drilled to a depth of about 170 feet below ground surface under the observation of a field engineer. The field engineer will determine the depth, sampler type, and frequency of sample collection during drilling based on data collected by previous geotechnical investigations at the site and observed conditions during drilling. After drilling the boring, the boring will be converted to a monitoring well. The driller will flush the borehole with biodegradable drilling mud and attach the VW piezometers to a sacrificial PVC pipe at the desired intervals. The driller will backfill the boring with a grout mix under the observation of the San Francisco Dept. of Public Health and San Francisco Public Works. After installing the VW piezometers and grouting the borehole, the new monitoring well will be covered by a monitoring well cover. Soil cuttings from the boring will be stored in 55-gallon steel drums and transported off-site for characterization and disposal by the driller. The purpose of the project is to gather data to measure soil compressibility.\n\nSub surface exploration consisting of 2 borings to=250 feet below the top of the basement mat foundation to obtain data for future foundation retrofit design, no exterior work","record_status":"Closed","project_address":"301 MISSION ST 35A 94105","block":"3719","lot":"266","child_id":"2018-004054ENV","open_date":"2018-03-21T00:00:00.000","close_date":"2018-10-03T00:00:00.000","building_permits":"201809139989","applicant":"Maffioli, Darcie","applicant_org":"SAGE Engineers, Inc.","assigned_to_planner":"Nicholas Foster","environmental_document_type":"Exemption","environmental_document_date":"4/2/2018","number_of_units_net":"0.0","number_of_market_rate_units":"0","number_of_affordable_units":"0","number_of_units_exist":"420","number_market_rate_units":"420","number_affordable_units_exist":"0","number_of_units_prop":"420","number_market_rate_units_1":"420","number_affordable_units_prop":"0","other_prj_desc":"CHECKED","pim_link":{"url":"https://sfplanninggis.org/pim?search=2018-004054PRJ"}},{"record_id":"2018-003445PRJ","record_type":"PRJ","project_name":"301 MISSION STREET","description":"Mat connection and shoring wall test project to help design a retrofit technique to stabilize the Millennium Tower against continued settlement.","record_status":"Open","project_address":"301 MISSION ST PH5 94105","block":"3719","lot":"439","child_id":"2018-003445ENV","open_date":"2018-03-09T00:00:00.000","applicant":"Clifford, Ryan","applicant_org":"Swinerton Builders","assigned_to_planner":"Virnaliza Byrd","environmental_document_type":"Exemption","environmental_document_date":"3/20/2018","number_of_units_net":"0.0","number_of_market_rate_units":"0","number_of_affordable_units":"0","number_of_units_exist":"0","number_market_rate_units":"0","number_affordable_units_exist":"0","number_of_units_prop":"0","number_market_rate_units_1":"0","number_affordable_units_prop":"0","other_prj_desc":"CHECKED","pim_link":{"url":"https://sfplanninggis.org/pim?search=2018-003445PRJ"}},{"record_id":"2019-002858PRJ","record_type":"PRJ","project_name":"301 Mission Street","description":"The purpose of the project is to characterize the soils in the area of work to inform preparation of a Site Mitigation Plan. As described in the Site Characterization Assessment Work Plan from AllWest Environmental dated January 30, 2019 (work plan), the proposed project would involve the collection of 36 soil samples from six soil borings within the sidewalks on Mission and Fremont Streets adjacent to 301 Mission Street (Millennium Tower) to comply with the Maher Ordinance. The approximate boring locations are shown on Figure 3 of the work plan. The boring locations have been modified pursuant to an amended Site Plan (Amended Figure 3 site plan dated March 8, 2019). Note that the boring locations shown on Amended Figure 3 are approximate to within 3 to 5 feet of the anticipated location. The borings would extend up to 30 feet below grade in accordance with a February 8, 2019 work plan authorization letter from the San Francisco Department of Public Health (DPH) regarding Maher Case Number 640. The first 5 feet of each boring would be completed with a hand auger, followed by advancement of the Geoprobe using a limited access track-mounted rig. The area of work around the rig would be approximately six feet by ten feet. Following the sampling, the casings and probes would be removed, the borings would be sealed with cement grout and the sidewalk restored. The anticipated duration of work is two days.\n\nThe project requires a Boring Permit from the San Francisco Department of Public Works (Public Works) and a Special Traffic Permit from the San Francisco Municipal Transportation Agency (SFMTA) to safely provide space within the public right-of-way for the boring equipment while ensuring safe path of travel for all modes in the vicinity of the subject boring activities.","record_status":"Closed","project_address":"301 MISSION ST PH6 94105","block":"3719","lot":"020","child_id":"2019-002858ENV","open_date":"2019-03-07T00:00:00.000","close_date":"2019-08-14T00:00:00.000","applicant":"Cunningham, Marc","applicant_org":"All West Environmental, Inc.","assigned_to_planner":"Virnaliza Byrd","environmental_document_type":"Exemption","environmental_document_date":"3/8/2019","number_of_units_net":"0.0","number_of_market_rate_units":"0","number_of_affordable_units":"0","number_of_units_exist":"0","number_market_rate_units":"0","number_affordable_units_exist":"0","number_of_units_prop":"0","number_market_rate_units_1":"0","number_affordable_units_prop":"0","facade_alt":"CHECKED","pim_link":{"url":"https://sfplanninggis.org/pim?search=2019-002858PRJ"}},{"record_id":"2023-001809PRJ","record_type":"PRJ","project_name":"301 MISSION STREET 48D & 48E","description":"Reasonable Modification to allow a temporary connection between two condominium units (48D and 48E).","record_status":"Closed","project_address":"301 MISSION ST 48D 94105","block":"3719","lot":"341","child_id":"2023-001809VAR","open_date":"2023-03-01T00:00:00.000","close_date":"2023-09-14T00:00:00.000","building_permits":"202303143620, 202303143623","applicant_org":"Goldstein, Gellman, Melbostad, Harris & McSparran, LLP","assigned_to_planner":"Vincent Page II","number_of_units_net":"0.0","number_of_market_rate_units":"0","number_of_affordable_units":"0","number_of_units_exist":"2","number_market_rate_units":"2","number_affordable_units_exist":"0","number_of_units_prop":"2","number_market_rate_units_1":"2","number_affordable_units_prop":"0","change_of_use":"No","demolition":"No","other_prj_desc":"CHECKED","residential_exist":"1730","parking_spaces_exist":"2","residential_prop":"37